    <DataNode elementId="Ceramides" textLabel="a ceramide" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="17761" dataSource="ChEBI" />
      <Graphics centerX="350" centerY="400" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment>A ceramide is a lipid molecule that is composed of |FRAME: Sphingoids| and |FRAME: Fatty-Acids|. Ceramides are found in high concentrations within the cell membrane and are one of the component lipids that make up |FRAME: Sphingomyelins sphingomyelin|, one of the major lipids in the lipid bilayer.</Comment>
